cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A corpus of prospective admission decisions from a replicated nf-core workflow"
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Chernov
    given-names: Alexander
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3198-2712"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doytsujin/ok-nfcore-admission-gate"
abstract: >-
  Thirty interleaved replicates of three arms of nf-core/demo v1.0.1 under
  Nextflow 24.10.5 and rootless podman, with a prospective admission gate wired
  into the engine so that a refused task never starts: an ungated baseline, a
  gated arm in which every task is admitted, and a refusal arm in which a
  declared condition is violated. 90 execution traces and 285 decision records,
  each carrying the verdict, the descriptor version, the refusal class where
  applicable, and every condition evaluated with its expected value, observed
  value and outcome — including conditions that passed on a refused request.
  The decision costs 11 microseconds at the median; the subprocess that delivers
  it costs 30 milliseconds. The refused step completed zero times in thirty
  replicates.
keywords:
  - admission control
  - workflow provenance
  - nextflow
  - nf-core
  - data governance
  - reproducibility
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
